            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0161" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A4a/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Williams</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-07T14:00:00+07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:44 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. In conversation yesterday at Foreign Office, the Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    informally expressed Siamese support of arrangement <pb facs="0162" n="42"
                        xml:id="pg42"/> for four-power agreement providing for common counsel in the
                    solution of problems in Pacific.</p>
                <p>Siam probably would welcome invitation to indicate diplomatic adherence to
                    agreement if the initiative in this connection came from the Government of the
                    United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
